Sure! Here is a simple example of a Node.js app that implements a CRUD REST API to manage employee data:

1. Create a new Node.js project and install the required dependencies:

```bash
mkdir employee-api
cd employee-api
npm init -y
npm install express mongoose body-parser
```

2. Create a `server.js` file with the following content:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const bodyParser = require('body-parser');
const mongoose = require('mongoose');

const app = express();
const PORT = 3000;

app.use(bodyParser.json());

mongoose.connect('mongodb://localhost:27017/employeeDB', { useNewUrlParser: true, useUnifiedTopology: true });

const Employee = mongoose.model('Employee', {
  name: String,
  title: String,
  department: String
});

// Create a new employee
app.post('/employees', async (req, res) => {
  const { name, title, department } = req.body;
  const employee = new Employee({ name, title, department });
  await employee.save();
  res.json(employee);
});

// Get all employees
app.get('/employees', async (req, res) => {
  const employees = await Employee.find();
  res.json(employees);
});

// Get an employee by ID
app.get('/employees/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const employee = await Employee.findById(req.params.id);
  res.json(employee);
});

// Update an employee by ID
app.put('/employees/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const employee = await Employee.findById(req.params.id);
  employee.set(req.body);
  await employee.save();
  res.json(employee);
});

// Delete an employee by ID
app.delete('/employees/:id', async (req, res) => {
  await Employee.findByIdAndDelete(req.params.id);
  res.send('Employee deleted successfully');
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});
```

3. Start the server by running the following command:

```bash
node server.js
```

You can now use tools like Postman to test the CRUD operations on the employee data. You can send POST requests to `http://localhost:3000/employees` to create a new employee, GET requests to `http://localhost:3000/employees` to get all employees, PUT requests to `http://localhost:3000/employees/:id` to update an employee, and DELETE requests to `http://localhost:3000/employees:id` to delete an employee.

