model_response:
You can create a new parameter P2(A,C) by iterating over sets A and C, and for each combination of A and C, finding the corresponding value of B using the one-to-one mapping from set B to C. Here's an example code in GAMS:

```
Set A, B, C;
Alias (A, i);
Alias (B, j);
Alias (C, k);

Parameter P1(A, B);
Parameter P2(A, C);

* Define the one-to-one mapping from set B to C
Mapping(j, k) = yes;

* Initialize P2
P2(A, C) = 0;

* Populate P2 using the one-to-one mapping
loop((A, C),
   P2(A, C) = sum(B, P1(A, B) * Mapping(B, C));
);
```

In this code, the `Mapping` parameter defines the one-to-one mapping from set B to set C. The `P2` parameter is initialized to zero and then populated by iterating over all combinations of A and C, and summing up the corresponding values from P1 using the one-to-one mapping.

