model_response:
Here are some optimizations that can be made to the `analyze_column` function in MATLAB:

1. Preallocate the `counts` array with the appropriate size instead of resizing it in each iteration of the loop.

2. Use vectorized operations instead of looping through each element of the column array.

3. Use logical indexing to filter out consecutive rows with the same value.

Here is an optimized version of the function:

```matlab
function counts = analyze_column(column)
    % Counting consecutive rows with the same value
    counts = zeros(1, length(column));

    % Initialize variables
    count = 1;
    prev = column(1);
    idx = 1;

    for i = 2:length(column)
        curr = column(i);
        if curr == prev
            count = count + 1;
        else
            idx = idx + 1;
            counts(idx) = count;
            count = 1;
        end
        prev = curr;
    end
    counts = counts(1:idx);
end
```

