To create a super sample rate FFT in Vitis HLS, you can follow these steps:

1. Define the input and output buffers for the FFT operation.
2. Set the FFT size and the super sampling rate.
3. Implement the FFT algorithm using the provided FFT library functions.
4. Compile the code using Vitis HLS tool.

Here is an example C code for a super sample rate FFT in Vitis HLS:

```c
#include <hls_fft.h>

#define FFT_SIZE 1024
#define SUPER_SAMPLING_RATE 4

// Define input and output buffers
complex<data_type> fft_in[FFT_SIZE];
complex<data_type> fft_out[FFT_SIZE];

void super_fft() {
    // Perform FFT operation with super sampling rate
    HLS_FFT<FFT_SIZE, data_type, data_type>(fft_in, fft_out, HLS_DIR_FORWARD, SUPER_SAMPLING_RATE);
}

int main() {
    // Initialize input buffer
    for(int i = 0; i < FFT_SIZE; i++) {
        fft_in[i].real = input_data[i];
        fft_in[i].imag = 0;
    }

    // Perform super sample rate FFT
    super_fft();

    // Output the result
    for(int i = 0; i < FFT_SIZE; i++) {
        cout << "Output FFT[" << i << "]: " << fft_out[i] << endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

Please note that this is just an example code and may need to be modified based on your specific requirements and the FFT library functions available in Vitis HLS. Make sure to check the documentation and guidelines provided by Xilinx for more detailed instructions on how to implement super sample rate FFT in Vitis HLS.

