To build a fully functioning website for selling clothes in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript without using any additional libraries, you can follow these steps:

1. Create the HTML structure for the website:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Clothing Store</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
<header>
<h1>Clothing Store</h1>
</header>
<main>
<section id="products">
<!-- Product listings will be dynamically generated here -->
</section>
</main>
<footer>
<p>&copy; 2022 Clothing Store</p>
</footer>
<script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

2. Create the CSS file to style the website (styles.css):

```css
body {
font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
margin: 0;
padding: 0;
}
header {
background-color: #f8f8f8;
padding: 10px;
text-align: center;
}
footer {
background-color: #f8f8f8;
padding: 10px;
text-align: center;
}
```

3. Create the JavaScript file to fetch and display products on the website (app.js):

```javascript
const products = [
{ name: "T-shirt", price: 20 },
{ name: "Jeans", price: 50 },
{ name: "Dress", price: 40 },
];

const renderProducts = () => {
const productsSection = document.getElementById("products");
products.forEach(product => {
const productDiv = document.createElement("div");
productDiv.classList.add("product");
productDiv.innerHTML = `
<h2>${product.name}</h2>
<p>Price: $${product.price}</p>
<button>Add to cart</button>
`;
productsSection.appendChild(productDiv);
});
};

renderProducts();
```

4. Implement additional features like adding products to a shopping cart, checkout functionality, etc. using plain JavaScript.

This is a basic outline of how you can build a clothing store website using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript without any additional libraries. You can customize the design, add more features, and improve the functionality as needed.

