You can write a JavaScript function to count the number of spaces in a text by using the following code:

```javascript
function countSpaces(text) {
  let count = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i++) {
    if (text[i] === ' ') {
      count++;
    }
  }

  return count;
}

// Example usage
const text = "This is a sample text with spaces";
console.log(countSpaces(text)); // Output: 5
```

In this function, we loop through each character in the input text and check if it is a space character. If it is, we increment a count variable. Finally, we return the total count of space characters found in the text.

