Sure! Here is a simple Unity code example for moving a 3D character with a point and click system using NavMesh:

```csharp
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.AI;

public class PointClickMovement : MonoBehaviour
{
    private NavMeshAgent agent;

    void Start()
    {
        agent = GetComponent<NavMeshAgent>();
    }

    void Update()
    {
        if (Input.GetMouseButtonDown(0))
        {
            Ray ray = Camera.main.ScreenPointToRay(Input.mousePosition);
            RaycastHit hit;
            if (Physics.Raycast(ray, out hit))
            {
                agent.SetDestination(hit.point);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

In this code example, we first get a reference to the `NavMeshAgent` component attached to the character in the `Start` method. Then, in the `Update` method, we check if the left mouse button is clicked. If it is, we cast a ray from the main camera to the mouse position on the screen, and if the ray hits something, we set the destination for the `NavMeshAgent` to that point.

