```javascript
// Simple implementation of a trainable AI algorithm in JavaScript

class AI {
  constructor() {
    this.weights = [Math.random(), Math.random()]; // Initialize random weights
    this.learningRate = 0.1;
  }

  predict(input) {
    const output = input.reduce((sum, value, index) => sum + value * this.weights[index], 0);
    return output;
  }

  train(input, target) {
    const prediction = this.predict(input);
    const error = target - prediction;

    // Update weights based on error
    this.weights = this.weights.map((weight, index) => weight + error * input[index] * this.learningRate);
  }
}

// Example usage
const ai = new AI();

const input = [1, 2]; // Input data
const target = 5; // Target output

console.log(`Initial prediction: ${ai.predict(input)}`);
ai.train(input, target);
console.log(`Updated prediction: ${ai.predict(input)}`);
```

This is a simple implementation of a trainable AI algorithm in JavaScript that uses a basic linear regression model. The AI class has a predict method that takes input data and returns the predicted output based on the current weights. The train method updates the weights based on the error between the predicted output and the target output. 

This implementation is small and straightforward, but it can be expanded upon and improved for more complex tasks and datasets.

