To create a webpage showing a rotating triangle that rotates clockwise every 1 second, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Here's an example code snippet:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Rotating Triangle</title>
<style>
    #triangle {
        width: 0;
        height: 0;
        border-left: 50px solid transparent;
        border-right: 50px solid transparent;
        border-bottom: 86.6px solid #f00; /* red triangle */
        position: absolute;
    }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="triangle"></div>
<script>
    const triangle = document.getElementById('triangle');
    let rotation = 0;

    setInterval(() => {
        rotation += 1;
        triangle.style.transform = `rotate(${rotation}deg)`;
    }, 1000);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

This code creates a webpage with a red equilateral triangle that rotates clockwise every 1 second. The triangle is created using CSS border properties and is rotated using JavaScript by incrementing the rotation angle every second. The triangle will continue to rotate indefinitely until the webpage is closed.

