Here is a PowerShell script that will show the nth number of the Fibonacci sequence:

```powershell
param(
    [Parameter(Mandatory=$true)]
    [int]$n
)

function Get-FibonacciNumber {
    param(
        [int]$n
    )

    if ($n -eq 0) {
        return 0
    }
    elseif ($n -eq 1) {
        return 1
    }
    else {
        return (Get-FibonacciNumber($n - 1) + Get-FibonacciNumber($n - 2))
    }
}

$nthFibonacciNumber = Get-FibonacciNumber -n $n
Write-Output "The $n-th number in the Fibonacci sequence is: $nthFibonacciNumber"
```

To use this script, save it to a file with a .ps1 extension (e.g., fibonacci.ps1) and then run it in PowerShell with the desired value of n as an argument. For example:

```
.\fibonacci.ps1 -n 10
```

This will output the 10th number in the Fibonacci sequence.

