Here are two example C functions that can be used to generate a score based on how far an input value is from a target value:

Function 1: Generate Score based on distance from target value
```c
// Function to generate a score based on how far an input value is from a target value
int generateScore(int inputValue, int targetValue) {
    int distance = abs(targetValue - inputValue); // Calculate the absolute distance from target
    int score = MAX_SCORE - distance; // Generate score based on distance

    return score;
}
```

Function 2: GA Fitness Function for Net Present Value
```c
// GA Fitness Function to measure how far a net present value is from a target value
float fitnessFunction(float netPresentValue, float targetValue) {
    float distance = fabs(targetValue - netPresentValue); // Calculate the absolute distance from target
    float fitness = 1 / (1 + distance); // Fitness function that gives higher fitness for values closer to the target

    return fitness;
}
```

These functions can be used in different scenarios such as optimizing parameters in a genetic algorithm or determining the performance of a model based on a target value.

