location / {
    if ($http_referer ~* (example.com)) {
        proxy_pass http://server1;
    }
    if ($http_referer ~* (anotherexample.com)) {
        proxy_pass http://server2;
    }
}
```

In this configuration, NGINX will proxy_pass requests to different backend servers based on the referer value. Make sure to replace "example.com" and "anotherexample.com" with the actual referer values you want to check for, and "http://server1" and "http://server2" with the backend server addresses you want to proxy_pass to. Additionally, keep in mind that using if statements in NGINX can be inefficient, so use them judiciously.

